{"law":"# CAMPAIGN qafreeze — pisco   (the law; the agent re-reads this every wake; rewrite, never append)\n\ncreated 2026-11-17 · kind **train** · root `/beegfs/scratch/user/hdejean/pisco` · window until **2027-02-15** (launches allowed through that day 23:59) · owner herve.dejean@naverlabs.com · wakes run `claude-opus-5`\n\n## Mission\nSuccessor of campaign 'freeze' (its report: /beegfs/scratch/user/hdejean/pisco/campaign_freeze/REPORT.md — not written yet; REPORT.json carries the same Settled list). Open at hand-off: nothing — the previous campaign settled every arm.\n**Question (owner, QUESTION.md; HANDOFF.md:66-70):** campaign freeze froze a compressor that had NEVER seen question-answering training. Can a compressor that HAS had one QA finetune then stay FROZEN while a fresh decoder LoRA is trained on the same rows? That is the case `<MEM>` caching needs: compress a collection once, train only the decoder afterwards.\n**Arm Q (what is tested):** the reference finetune recipe of 184778 / 184780 with ONE change — it starts from a hybrid init: R's own `compressor/` + `connector.pt` (QA-trained) with R's `decoder_state.pt` replaced by the stage-2 decoder (`expQ/archq3/pt_mm_5M_spread/model/decoder_state.pt`, R's own starting point), run with `+model_config_overrides.freeze_compressor=true`, so only the decoder LoRA trains. GUESS: the hybrid is assembled by copying R's model dir and swapping that one file — the only route that needs no new code, since `PISCO.from_pretrained` reads exactly `decoder_state.pt`, `compressor/compressor_state.pt`, `connector.pt` and `config.json` (pisco/model.py:1376-1405); the two configs differ only in `connector_out_norm` / its init / the image-processor path (`expQ/ft_mm_4b_184778/model/config.json:11-12,24`), and R's config travels with R's connector.\n**The deciding number:** paired judge accuracy (Qwen3-8B rubric judge `scripts/judge_mm_docqa.py`; `scripts/paired_judge.py` = bootstrap 95% CI + McNemar), Q − R of the same seed, n = 1,500 questions per set, seeds 42 (vs 184778) and 43 (vs 184780). GUESS: seed 43 freezes 184780's compressor (the seed-43 reference), so each seed is one self-contained replicate; the owner's question names only 184778.\nGating sets: documents `eval_data/mm_docqa_1500_1m`, photos `eval_data/mm_naturalqa_1500`, MRQA text `eval_data/text_mrqa_ood_1500`. HotpotQA `eval_data/text_hotpotqa_1500` is reported, not gating (freeze's text loss sat there: −3.0 / −2.8 / −3.6, QUESTION.md:11).\nPASS = every gating set ≥ −2 pt with no CI wholly below 0 at both seeds → the `<MEM>` cache is built (a hand-off; see On acceptance). FAIL = ≤ −3 pt with the CI wholly below 0 at both seeds.\n**Reference numbers, same instrument** (campaign_freeze/STATE.md:66-85, n = 1,500 per set): R documents .610 / .615, photos .673 / .685, MRQA .718 / .724, HotpotQA .603 / .593; F (stage-2 compressor + connector frozen, decoder only) − R documents −.028 / −.035 / −.041; A1 (compressor only frozen) − R −.029 / −.039 / −.
